=== E. short-sale margin (Reg T 150% / FINRA 4210(c)(2)-(3)) ===
  short 100 sh @ $50: CMV $5,000
  Reg T initial 150% of CMV = $7,500 (100% if a qualifying convertible is held = $5,000)
  do not invent 'deposit 150% cash on top of the short proceeds'
  FINRA maintenance at $50 (>= $5): max($5 x 100 = $500, 30% x $5,000 = $1,500) = $1,500
  short 100 sh @ $4: CMV $400
  FINRA maintenance below $5: max($2.50 x 100 = $250, 100% x $400 = $400) = $400
  contrast, 100 sh @ $2: max($250, 100% x $200 = $200) = $250
  contrast, 100 sh @ $10: max($500, 30% x $1,000 = $300) = $500
  long initial/maintenance remain 50%/25% as already taught; house rates may be stricter
assertions passed: 4/4
ASSERT_short_margin_ok
disclaimer: strategy-based short-margin toy; house rates may be stricter; learning only
=== F. Rule 10b-16: written credit-term statements at opening, at least quarterly, and generally thirty (30) days notice of changes ===
10b-16(a): It shall be unlawful for any broker or dealer to extend credit, directly or
  indirectly, to any customer in connection with any securities transaction unless such
  broker or dealer has established procedures to assure that each customer:
  (a)(1) is given or sent at the time of opening the account, a written statement or
  statements disclosing the official (i)-(vii) items
  official (a)(1) telephone proviso exists: the account may be opened by telephone if
  the information is orally communicated at that time and the required written
  statement or statements are sent immediately thereafter; this is not a claim that
  there is never a written statement when an account is opened by telephone
  official (a)(1)(i)-(vii) exist; this toy is not that catalog
  (a)(2) is given or sent a written statement or statements, at least quarterly, for
  each account in which credit was extended
10b-16(b): the customer shall have been given not less than thirty (30) days written
  notice of such changes, except that no such prior notice shall be necessary where
  such changes are required by law
  if a change results in a lower interest charge, notice may be given within a
  reasonable time after the effective date of the change
